{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Canonical current-tree publication policy. Exact public exceptions win over deny rules; deny rules win over explicit public permits; unmatched paths are unclassified and refused by the projector.",
  "authoring_rules": {
    "public_exceptions": "An exception is an UNCONDITIONAL publish: it is evaluated before every deny rule, including **/*.pem, **/.env and **/*.local.md. Add one only when a broad deny would otherwise strip a specific file that must ship, and keep it as narrow as the file. A subtree exception (dir/**) makes that whole subtree unpublishable-by-policy-only, so nothing generated into it can ever be caught by a deny rule. shared/capabilities/public/** was such an entry and was removed on 2026-08-11: it changed no tracked classification (that subtree already matched shared/** under `public`), while it silently force-published anything a generator wrote there.",
    "default_deny": "A public rule is a permit, not a hint. An unmatched path is refused and named in the projection receipt; adding a new top-level namespace, document, or tool requires an explicit public permit.",
    "tools_run_output": "Only enumerated publishable tool families are permitted. Within them, run output is still recognised by ROLE NAME at ANY DEPTH in EITHER FORM -- `tools/**/<role>/**` for the directory form and `tools/**/<role>.*` for the file form. Both halves remain load-bearing defense in depth.",
    "personal_work": "The public repo publishes the squad SYSTEM only. Any project tree that is not the squad system (everything under projects/**, apps/**, and any future sibling) gets an EXPLICIT deny rule, never reliance on default-deny. Default-deny does refuse them today, but that is protection by absence of a rule: it disappears silently the moment a broad public permit happens to match, and no gate fires. Deny beats permit here, so the explicit rule survives allowlist edits. Added 2026-09-14 after a large tracked tree was found blocked only by fall-through; generalised 2026-09-19 when the last project tree moved to its own repository."
  },
  "public_capability_state": {
    "bounty": {
      "status": "documentation-only",
      "notice": "This projection publishes transferable workflow documentation. It does not assert that referenced capabilities are included or operational; verify availability before use.",
      "withheld": [
        "Capability availability is not asserted by this projection."
      ]
    }
  },
